","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test/verification that the byte cap actually enforces on the deployed filesystem — e.g. writing past the ceiling is prevented or reclaimed — not only that the quota/timer config is present.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: 'has documented age cleanup and an actual enforced size ceiling on the Gerrit host'","AC test line names only 'cleanup/quota/timer config' — configuration presence, not enforcement behavior","Design Ambiguity notes 'on root/XFS a separate byte-cap mechanism may be needed' — whether the cap enforces is exactly the uncertain, load-bearing behavior"],"finding":"The load-bearing claim of the plan is 'an actual enforced size ceiling', yet the test acceptance criterion only names 'cleanup/quota/timer config' testing plus metric/alarm wiring. Config-shape tests verify that the mechanism is configured, not that the byte cap actually enforces (that writing past the ceiling on the deployed XFS root is prevented/reclaimed). This risks closing green while the cap does not actually bound growth under fill.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe8823c8dcb52cee1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'Targeted tests cover cleanup/quota/timer config, metric emission, and alarm wiring.'","norm_id":"n3a986ae5a4e32d41","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A quota is configured but does not enforce on the actual root/XFS filesystem; config tests pass, generator fills disk anyway, and only the alarm (not the cap) reacts"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an enforcement test